{"seq":19,"trial_id":"shared-brain-access-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-told-labelled-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-22T14:34:58.635Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"41450ba77fa34c205d6ad8e828c48159787e23ad573029b0db1d15be8a314a58","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all six of Moss's notes in the shared files. Two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025: the Eau Claire gatehouse kiosk wasn't sending SMS bay assignments for doors 14–18 on the 04:00 shift. Support patched it on 4 Oct, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that it was fixed. The note also has a follow-up to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it for gatehouse barcode scanners not reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nMoss's other North notes on QFL (the 2025-09-14 pipeline digest and the 2026-03-23 renewal check-in) don't have ticket numbers, and the two Central notes don't mention QFL.\n\nBefore #4419 goes in the weekly notes: Marcus's handoff note (members/marcus-lindqvist/notes/2025-07-14-marcus-q2-expansion-wrap.md, his note, not Moss's) describes #4419 as \"Gate 3 printer lag\", a BOL printout delay. That doesn't match Moss's scanner description, so you may want to check the real ticket. Also, \"Quarendon Freightways\" (one r) in Marcus's competitive intel note is a different company and not a customer, so I left it out."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
